{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages","id":988607,"title":"Has anyone thought up their own lineages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T19:39:47-07:00","id":988607,"title":"Has anyone thought up their own lineages?","content":"I so wanted to call them bloodlines, but that has another meaning in Requiem.<br /> <br /> What I'm specifically wonder about is if anyone else here has done family trees for their chronicles and characters, showing who Embraced who and detailing what one particular strain of the curse has looked like over the long centuries. I've wanted to do a 'generational' chronicle for ages now (since before Requiem for Rome, but doubly so since that came out) and figured I'd see if anybody else had taken a shot at it before I dove in and explored five centuries of Mekhet shenanigans. I'm toying with whether or not I want to string together the various Dark Eras or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:54:07-07:00","id":989473,"title":"","content":"I have. Most of my Venture characters belong to my custom Nicomachus bloodline.<br /> <br /> It has no special powers but most experience a similar pattern in life. They are embraced as warrior-poets, possessing strong will, keen intellect and aggressive personalities. During their neonate years, they begin to feel a desire to campaign and conquer; to expand and discover the new. In our saturated world, this does feel harder but most express the beast's wanderlust in some way. Leading a communist party from a local environment to key regional player is a more underground expansion but is sufficient. I prefer being more overt though. After their warring, they oft find themselves in new locals, where they settle down and become local Venture, winning and building, until their childer leave them too.<br /> <br /> 'Copyright' claim: You have permission to use them. Just be sure to send me a PM so I can enjoy a sense of pride in your desire to play my creations and so I can add new members and their adventures to the family tree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  copyright. 10-18-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:53:27-07:00","id":989494,"title":"","content":"There's also Dynasty Membership if you want families with a mechanical impact that are not actual Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T13:27:49-07:00","id":989503,"title":"","content":"Just happened to read this thread after seeing the new trailer for the Assassin's Creed movie. It's not the sort of thing I typically do because I actually kind of hate excessive backstory unless it's definitely, actively going to come up in-game, but mucking about in history using Sires and their Childer sounds like fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T05:20:28-07:00","id":990909,"title":"","content":"Last game i played, where the PCs were sort of elders would most certainly count. While the family trees seen wouldn't go too deep - sires &amp; childer mostly, sometimes sires, childer &amp; grandchilder - they sort of spread out in interesting ways. Add to that the fact the older a vampire gets, the more time it had to make other childer (that will have formed ideas/plans/worldviews/connections of their own) and the possible interactions of the elder and/or its varied descendants with the &quot;families&quot; of other kindred, allying, competing, destroying or romancing with them, their sires, childer, rivals &amp; etc and after sometime you end up with a surprisingly loaded minefield of associations.<br /> <br /> For a PC example, my character, through a process involving more spur-of-the-moment rolls and the improvisational interpretation of them, was defined as having embraced 3 (known) childer in his 120+ years of nightlife, all of them victims of all too human violence &quot;rescued&quot; through the embrace.<br /> <br /> The first, Melquior, was a bohemian investigative journalist in 1910s Rio de Janeiro with whom Baltazar, himself being a journalist, poet and ex-guerilla fighter dead for 20 years at the time, struck a friendship with, what resulted on his being close by when a group of thugs assaulted them and mortally wounded Melquior, whom Baltazar embraced on impulse. While it started fine, subtle differences of perspective and personal experience - like Baltazar being the sireless product of a strix-esque pact (different critter, different clan) that literally rose from an unmarked grave after being executed and hacked to pieces for opposing the government in a revolt in Santa Catarina - would drive some wedges and lead them in different directions, Melquior becoming a rabid leading Carthian (and nuisance to a number of elders), while his sire become a eccentric though well-established figure of the Ordo Dracul. In fact, due to their stormy relationship and Melquior being himself an ancilla/near-elder already, not all kindred that know of them are aware of the precise family connection, seeing them as either (barely) amicable rivals or brothers.<br /> <br /> <br /> The second, Gaspar, is a fruit of Baltazar's &quot;nomad years&quot; (mid-10s to 50s), when he got tired of petty intrigue and rumour-mongering and left the city for a number of decades to travel across the country and beyond under the guise of a travelling circus freak show (and map obscure dragon's nest and what inhabited them or not, across the continent in the proccess), a runaway boy that ended being sort of adopted into the circus during the 40s. In one of those travels a wandering serial killer crossed their paths and disapeared with the boy, whose buried body in an unmarked grave in the woods would be found by a grieving Baltazar in the edge of frenzy, what lead to a beast-spurred desperate post mortem embrace of the boy, his frenzied return to quasi-life and the two of them would them proceed to track down and give the maniac some the most harrowing and final nights of his life. This incident also lead to the Kanaima, the peculiar devil-cats that made Baltazar, coming to visit their &quot;grandchild&quot;, pleased with one that took so quickly well to the heart of predator and monster &quot;unlike the soft talkative one in the big city&quot;, alerting Baltazar (a little too late) of one grievous error/omission on his part when he had mostly left Melquior and Rio de Janeiro. Already seeing Baltazar and his wife, the witch Ofelia, as the parents he wanted to stay with, the boy settled them into a macabre family of sorts and they adapted to the new situation with surprisingly little trouble and has become a Dragon, much like dad, in the following decades.<br /> <br /> <br /> The third and final childe, Maria, came to be in the decades after Baltazar &amp; family decided to settle down once more in Rio de Janeiro, a young woman that attracted the attention of Ofelia in the 70s, becoming a friend, apprentice and occasional lover of the witch, who had been seriously considering initiating her, when life decided to intervene and Maria was disappeared with by the military, much like many other university students or young people of the period, for connections (factual or spurious) with the armed resistance movements.<br /> Ofelia found out their suspicions through Maria's parents and guilt-tripped/tricked Baltazar in hunting down her whereabouts, to rescue or avenge her. The result was some quick, heated talks with Melquior, a number of younger kindred he had mentored/tutored in the past decades, associates in the Ordo and other covenants disatisfied with how the military's &quot;witch hunts&quot; among intellectual and student circles were messing with the herds and prospective of a number of them, inadvertently sparking a series of quick, fast and very, very, brutally messy attacks against hideouts of the DOPS (the political police of the military junta) as those kindred &quot;rescued&quot; childer to be and/or killed a number of DOPS grunts out of spite, not to mention one or two tales of the group embrace of prisioners who would make their first meals out of their tormentors. Thankfully the political climate, not to mention the interrogators/torturers own penchant for secrecy and for isolated, out-of-the way hideout was probably the main reason the whole thing did not become a masquerade disaster.<br /> <br /> It also lead to some hefty dissatisfaction with and pressure in the Invictus, that had the strongest ties/investment in the military) and the eventual intervention of the prince of the time, a Crone worshipper, who showed considerable (self-serving) leniency to the dissatisfied/rebelious kindred grievance, in no small part because the tension that had built up and sparked from the situation gave him very convenient justification he desired to take down a peg or two of the Invictus' growing influence for his own sake.<br /> <br /> Things eventually calmed down and Maria, the childe of Baltazar (though some suspect her real sire is Melquior and Baltazar assumed her because he had a much better relation with prince &amp; sheriff) would be lead by her own sorcerous leanings from life toward the Crone, but her along with a number of people coming from this wave of impassionated, violent embraces of the period, would also form a clique/social circle of sorts beyond their family or covenant relations, a generation of kindred informally known as &quot;crias de chumbo&quot; (childer of lead, a reference to the &quot;years of lead&quot;, the harshest period of political persecution in Brasil).<br /> <br /> At the start i just made some rough basics, to which me, the ST and the rest of the group (the Daeva Carthian PC was also an ally of Melquior, Maria was a pupil of the Ventrue Crone PC) would add or flesh out bits and pieces as the chronicle advanced, like Eric the Daeva assuming as Melquior's &quot;godfather&quot;/mentor as a favor to Baltazar when he decided to go nomad, what leads to some kindred thinking he is Melquior's sire instead, or how in one of his occasional visits through Rio de Janeiro back then sire and childe ended up in opposing sides of an armed revolt in the 30s that caused the fall of a prince, how Isabelle the Ventrue's present nightclub was Baltazar's between the 50-70s, when he changed domains in the city, which would later gain context with the whole &quot;childer of lead&quot; mess - that initially was just about Baltazar &amp; Maria, but then evolved into something else as one or two references to kindred with a bias against the Invictus due to similar experiences settled in and it inspired me to write up something of a &quot;period event&quot; and &quot;mending of bridges&quot; of sorts between Baltazar and Melquior and their fighting on opposing sides of a praxis seizure in the late 30s.<br /> <br /> And that's just crap relating directly to my character and his childer - and he does have at least one unmentioned grandchilder - things can get pretty convoluted when one tries to map other kindred, their childer, sires and who is still active, in torpor, destroyed or possible agendas. Pretty engrossing and entertaining overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:18:02-07:00","id":997447,"title":"","content":"Well I had a lineage of Daeva vampires and it goes like this:<ul><li>Adrien English (newest Embracee)</li> <li>Childe of Michael Riordan</li> <li>Childe of Rachel Summers</li> <li>Childe of ???</li> <li>Childe of Pietro Veneziano</li> <li>Childe of Vienna<br /> <br /> Long story short, Pietro was a handsome Venetian painter during the Renaissance, who was Embraced by a Daeva that adored him, she was killed by Inquisitors and he eventually ended up in the US, Embracing a line of borderline sociopaths and had to deal with their crap. He is surprisingly humane for a Daeva Elder, and is probably seeking Golconda by now.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:29:19-07:00","id":997451,"title":"","content":"I always loved this lineage fluff, especially in Masquerade when all Kindred in the world were connected through a single progenitor, now it seems so far apart and vague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:32:21-07:00","id":997454,"title":"","content":"I agree. Much harder to pull off, and less reason to. Unless you're building dynasties. I suppose the elder book might get into it, as their childer and childer's childer may be important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:43:55-07:00","id":998613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=997451#post997451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always loved this lineage fluff, especially in Masquerade when all Kindred in the world were connected through a single progenitor, now it seems so far apart and vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sincerely i don't see much of a problem. A lack of mythology/family trees is corrected by development of them, that much simpler in a setting with greater freedom from expectations about what should be fact, myth or convenient falsehood. No need for canon inconsistencies like Tyler as an ancilla in 1100s england while Critias and Khalid, kindred who actually have the background to justify book appearances, are utterly ignored by Constantinople By Night for example, or flame wars about bits of fiction treated as dogma and even worse flame wars about bits like Mithras being a literal childe of the Ventrue Antediluvian or &quot;just&quot; a very successful diablerist that remade his own history and that of the clan itself from the middle ages onwards, among other stuff.<br /> <br /> No presumption of canon/myth/truth means among other things that not only the ST but the players themselves have complete freedom to develop their own chronicle's mythology in tandem and progressively, adding or cutting bits as the narrative offers hooks, hints and scattered bits that are then exploited or tinkered with. It even allows for one to make different takes of a myth or wholy different vampiric backstories from game to game, or even between story arcs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=997454#post997454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. Much harder to pull off, and less reason to. Unless you're building dynasties. I suppose the elder book might get into it, as their childer and childer's childer may be important.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so, because there's no encyclopedia of NPCs to reference as sires, grandsires &amp; etc? Personally, i don't care overly much for that kind of official validation and actually much enjoy fleshing out the background of a chronicle from a mix of book material, ideas my own and whatever the players feel like throwing at me. City books, adventures and other supplements are first and foremost tools, if a NPC is used as is or simply as an archetype/template a ST or player milks &amp; tinkers with is a matter of taste and personal preferences in the end.<br /> <br /> Actually fleshing out the bits on one's own instead of just connecting a ready set of dots also means more personal investment of the writer, and on the baggage one actually needs or wants, to boot.<br /> <br /> So i can't really say i agree or even really see in what way the lack of Caine/Lilith/Bloody Santa makes things &quot;harder to pull off&quot; and much more importantly &quot;less reason to&quot;, honestly.<br /> <br /> A book on elders and making up dinasties might be entertaining and useful, but for all i care examples from novels (be they from CoD, oWod, Anne Rice, Brian Lumley or whomever), comics, films, tv series &amp; cartoons or even literal dinasties - fictional or historical - with little to no relation to vampires, can provide one with a framework of ideas to work from.<br /> <br /> My two cents of thought and if it kind of turned out in something of a rant, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:54:38-07:00","id":998615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=997451#post997451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always loved this lineage fluff, especially in Masquerade when all Kindred in the world were connected through a single progenitor, now it seems so far apart and vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you need a single progenitor to create lineages? Wouldn't it help since with &quot;1 progenitor&quot; you will always go back to &quot;original vampire&quot; for every single character, but with multiple potential origins you can make a lineage that goes from your character (or the vampires they've sired... or the vampires those vampires sired, etc.) back through the ages to a specific progenitor who did unique x thing. Having a lineage doesn't seem very prestigious if in the end if Everyone has the same ancestor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T23:20:44-07:00","id":998630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=998613#post998613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so, because there's no encyclopedia of NPCs to reference as sires, grandsires &amp; etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Because Masquerade limited things by having a set amount of Generations, with the first three already 'called for.' Since players tended to be 12th generation in Dark Ages, and 13th in Modern Nights. That leaves a whopping 8-9 names between your character and their clan progenitor. Considering the importance of ones sire and the egotism of elders, it makes sense for their names to be shared down the line even if all you know about your great great grand sire was that their name was Pard.<br /> <br /> Requiem has no such limitation. No one knows the origin. How far back would you go? Then there's the fact that clan, or at least lineage, wasn't as important a factor in the game. One vampire may have been Embraced two hundred years ago, but a neonate with drive and focus can best them at every aspect of their Requiem. So age, by itself, isn't necessarily a determinator of power. Which leaves you with a list of names and why is that list of names important? Who was so worth remembering that a thousand years later, a neonate is going to know every link between her and them? Keep in mind, without a generation, there could literally be a thousand undead names between them.<br /> <br /> Then you have the incidental things. Fog of Eternity can leave vampires forgetting their names, admittedly less of a problem in second edition. Posthumous and other weird Embraces that leave a line unclear. 'Siblings,' of all those people, who may have at one point taken a plane and flown somewhere because there's no sect saying they can't and they might have spawned an entire new bloodline.<br /> <br /> Reading the clanbooks was a joy. One of the best things about it was seeing how little vampires actually knew. One of the other best things about it was seeing how much they made up to conceal their ignorance. Requiem's great like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, i don't care overly much for that kind of official validation and actually much enjoy fleshing out the background of a chronicle from a mix of book material, ideas my own and whatever the players feel like throwing at me. City books, adventures and other supplements are first and foremost tools, if a NPC is used as is or simply as an archetype/template a ST or player milks &amp; tinkers with is a matter of taste and personal preferences in the end.<br /> <br /> Actually fleshing out the bits on one's own instead of just connecting a ready set of dots also means more personal investment of the writer, and on the baggage one actually needs or wants, to boot.<br /> <br /> So i can't really say i agree or even really see in what way it the lack of Caine/Lilith/Bloody Santa makes things &quot;harder to pull off&quot; and much more importantly &quot;less reason to&quot;, honestly. </div> </div> </div>Did my explanation help? I get the fun that can be had in developing your own character's past, but from a Storyteller standpoint, maybe it's lazy but I'm not going to make a chain from every NPC to the first human and beyond, as it's possible and even likely that there's pre-human sources of vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-05-2016, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:33:05-07:00","id":998726,"title":"","content":"I only bother with lineages if its relevant to plot. IE - your relationships are within the same city, or really close nearby. But list off long dead or far away ancestors? Nope. Certain branches of the Invictus are the only ones who really care about that, and even that is pushing it with the 2e version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:13:53-07:00","id":998901,"title":"","content":"I made a powerful Ventrue dynasty in Tokyo named after the god of the moon (Tsukuyomi) with a friend of mine for some unaligned characters we had in mind. They were steeped in all kinds of history and complex traditions, and we wrote up a full family tree of vampires brought into the line from start to modern times. Among their traditions was various 'family gatherings' during events like new Embraces, reaching Ancilla status, and marriage. Sires were expected to be very involved with their childe's activities and essentially take them on as adopted children.<br /> <br /> Marriage was another big thing in the line - for ritual purposes each Ventrue vampire in the line was supposed to pick a mortal and ghoul them, and then join with them as a spouse. It was to reinforce the line's 'familial integrity,' in honor of the line founder lost love, so the line is full of the twisted co-dependent relationships of various kinds of immortal blood addicts. I think we detailed 4 generations with the family tree, back to the 1400s. They were pretty conservative about new embraces, but the line's also full of ancient ghouls and some unacknowledged 'bastard' vampires too. <br /> <br /> They're a bit provincial as vampires go, focusing on controlling specific territories rather than seeking wider influence over the workings of the city and Zaibatsu. We joked that one of the Ancilla in the line is 'The Shogun of the Shopping Mall' since he essentially controlled the owners of every business in the place and made contacts through them, working to keep the place open late hours into the evening, but he and his ghoul bride rarely looked past their current holdings and just focused on securing what they already had. This was the sire of the Neonate who got us started thinking on the entire thing; said Neonate is starting by running a manga cafe from behind the scenes and trying to expand influence over the neighborhood from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T16:29:08-07:00","id":998938,"title":"","content":"I usually make lineages even if they aren't extensive. The game mechanics involving vampire relationships are designed in such a way that one vampire automatically irritates the hell out of another other just by merely existing and its so easy to victimize each other with such impunity that I personally find it unbelievable that they would exist in close proximity to another unless they have family nearby or there are deus ex machina elements in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:52:50-08:00","id":1010453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=998630#post998630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Because Masquerade limited things by having a set amount of Generations, with the first three already 'called for.' Since players tended to be 12th generation in Dark Ages, and 13th in Modern Nights. That leaves a whopping 8-9 names between your character and their clan progenitor. Considering the importance of ones sire and the egotism of elders, it makes sense for their names to be shared down the line even if all you know about your great great grand sire was that their name was Pard.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as one wishes things to go - or not. what makes 10, 12, 15 or 20 generations to cover the time between modern nights and untold millenia down to &quot;the dawn of history&quot;, whenever that is, supposing the Caine mythos was even true, what it didn't really have to? Also, diablerie puts a serious monkeywrench in the generation x lineage matter. Also, not like Cain was the only person ever cursed by heavens in mythology or even the Bible, for that matter. Topics like &quot;Lilith as the first vampire&quot; are just one obvious example of how artificial the whole conceit is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=998630#post998630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem has no such limitation. No one knows the origin. How far back would you go? Then there's the fact that clan, or at least lineage, wasn't as important a factor in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem establishes no such thing - but it's a feature, not a bug, imho. It lets you establish the origin of vampires as far in the past - or close to the present - as one <b>wishes </b>it to be, be it the storyteller when making up its setting, or an enterprising <b>player </b>when adding its own spin to the tale.<br /> <br /> A ST - and his or her players, have <b>exactly </b>what they <b>care</b> to develop to their chronicle, with no need whatsoever to fill blanks in some hypothetical list if it does not serve the story - and <b>who</b> is Pard anyway, beside some name in the sheet of Arnulf in Transylvania By Night, uh? <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> A name is a name, but if a lineage is of my own creation i can make <b>each </b>part of it story relevant, or leave whole sections of it obscured and undefined to be adressed and developed during the game, as some narrative need, hook or new idea comes up. There's freedom and dynamism in that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=998630#post998630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One vampire may have been Embraced two hundred years ago, but a neonate with drive and focus can best them at every aspect of their Requiem. ]So age, by itself, isn't necessarily a determinator of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, is that different from enterprising neonates, diablerist or just lucky to be low gen, how? <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=998630#post998630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which leaves you with a list of names and why is that list of names important? Who was so worth remembering that a thousand years later, a neonate is going to know every link between her and them? Keep in mind, without a generation, there could literally be a thousand undead names between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters the fact they actually relate to <i>NPCs directly connected to the game story/city one plays in</i> - that right there is far more than can be said about 90% of any canon NPCs ever until one tinkers with them, no?<br /> Even if actually destroyed (what does not have to be the case, as Torpor, faking one's death, leaving on some personal journey spiritual or otherwise &amp; etc are always possible), such individuals actions and memory can influence the backstory of one's setting or some of its characters in a number of ways, as they leave descendants, who may carry on with grudges, rivalries, alliances, complicated romance/family issues and so on. Book material is fun, but i want as much to create and play, more so, as to read about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=998630#post998630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you have the incidental things. Fog of Eternity can leave vampires forgetting their names, admittedly less of a problem in second edition. Posthumous and other weird Embraces that leave a line unclear. 'Siblings,' of all those people, who may have at one point taken a plane and flown somewhere because there's no sect saying they can't and they might have spawned an entire new bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is part of what i love about the current setup. to put it bluntly, think of the same joy you described in seeing how little vampires actually knew and how much they made up to conceal their ignorance. These things and more can contribute, much, to exactly this. The lack of certainty means &quot;the begining of vampires/clan X/bloodline Y&quot; can be told in dozens of different ways across the ages and places, some true, some false (or maybe all false or more strangely, all true) and questions about the Fog make it so that it's hard to say for sure what's an elders delirium or <i>what is an actually quite true tale but so weird it sounds like madness or myth</i>.<br /> <br /> PS. Sorry for taking so long to answer, life stuff got in the way for a week or two and then it took some time to get the head anywhere close to back to gear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T10:20:46-08:00","id":1010694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988607-has-anyone-thought-up-their-own-lineages?p=1010453#post1010453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem establishes no such thing - but it's a feature, not a bug, imho. It lets you establish the origin of vampires as far in the past - or close to the present - as one wishes it to be, be it the storyteller when making up its setting, or an enterprising player when adding its own spin to the tale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it was a bug. It's a whole point of the game. Requiem is not about what some vampire did hundreds of years ago. It's about what your character is doing now that they're a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A ST - and his or her players, have exactly what they cares to develop to their chronicle, with no need whatsoever to fill blanks in some hypothetical list if it does not serve the story - and who is Pard anyway, beside some name in the sheet of Arnulf in Transylvania By Night, uh? <br /> <br /> A name is a name, but if a lineage is of my own creation i can make each part of it story relevant, or leave whole sections of it obscured and undefined to be adressed and developed during the game, as some narrative need, hook or new idea comes up. There's freedom and dynamism in that. </div> </div> </div>What you're talking about is background. I said there was less reason to do lineages, and based on my aforementioned 'the game is about you, now' there's still less reason to do a background that doesn't involve you and instead relies entirely on the actions of NPCs before the game even started. Yes, that level of background can be important to you or your character, but that doesn't mean it's necessary for all or even most characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an aside, is that different from enterprising neonates, diablerist or just lucky to be low gen, how? </div> </div> </div>John is a 150 year old vampire. He's excelled beyond the limits of his sire, who was only a 10 year old vampire who reached the Final Death when John was two years into his Requiem. Why should John tell his childe anything about his sire? There is no important link between him and some clan progenitor. There is no customary 'honoring your sire' system. Even aside from that, any vampire can just say, 'It started with me,' just like Dracula did, especially because sometimes it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, for starters the fact they actually relate to NPCs directly connected to the game story/city one plays in - that right is far more than can be said about 90% of any canon NPCs ever until one tinkers with them, no?<br /> <br /> Even if actually destroyed (what does not have to be the case, as Torpor, faking one's death, leaving on some personal journey spiritual or otherwise &amp; etc are always possible), such individuals actions and memory can influence the backstory of one's setting or some of its characters in a number of ways, as they leave descendants, who may carry on with grudges, rivalries, alliances, complicated romance/family issues and so on. Book material is fun, but i want as much to create and play, more so, as to read about it. </div> </div> </div>Again, the game is about the here and now, your character. Nothing's keeping you from doing all that, and if it's something you want to do you should. But it's not the basis of the game the way it was in Masquerade. Thus there's less reason to do it outside of your personal desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:14:48-08:00","id":1010715,"title":"","content":"I always try to have several Dynasties in the Requiem Chronicles I write. It adds some delicious history to the city setting and gives a wonderful feeling of obligation and paranoia to those PCs who decide to be a part of a lineage. <br /> <br /> That, and creating the dark secrets of the elders of the Dynasties is always a blast. For no Kindred reaches the age of an elder without having to do some terrible things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:50:09-08:00","id":1010734,"title":"","content":"Folks today--you and I--don't spend much time remembering and recounting our ancestors. They're not around, not doing things, and our self-worth is not wrapped up our family history by and large. It's tied to education, and employment, and accomplishment of same. Mostly--bear with me.<br /> <br /> In older days, especially when oral history was the main way of explaining the world and How Things Are, family and ancestry was <i>everything</i>. It served as a shorthand to explain to others who you were so they could make an immediately judgement regarding your worth and expected behavior. Nobles were nobles because they came from recognized lineages, with ancestors who had done X and Y, and were therefore expected to uphold the quality of their line--if they did not it brought shame on both themselves and their lineage, and thus the lineage members would act to punish reprobates.<br /> <br /> Nobodies. Nithings--nothings. Sons (or daughters) of no-one were both expected little of and dangerous because they had no one standing behind them to act as a control or brake. If they F'ed up and caused trouble who would recompense? Who would bring the troublemaker into line? The local authorities and that's all. Peasants away from home would fall into this category, and that's one reason nobles didn't trust them and restricted their travel. (Peasants near home, in England at least, had to belong to local justice collectives for all these reasons--to ensure someone was going to bring them into line/pay up if trouble started.)<br /> <br /> So, flip this over onto vampires, and you see the same reasoning at work. If someone walks in and says they're &quot;Daffyd ap Rhodry ap Geraint ap Mithras ap Veddartha&quot; he's telling you two main things: A) he's noble enough to understand his lineage and recognizes it as important, and B) he's giving you a list of references/insurers in case things go south. It's polite to do this. It ensures you can process whether the night is likely to go up in flames because you or someone in your court has issues with &quot;Daffyd's&quot; lineage, or conflicts further back between mutual sires. And if you think Geraint is a tool, you can assume Rhodry probably is and Daffyd as well.<br /> <br /> VtM made lineages a core part of the game because of Generation, but also because it reinforced the globe-spanning metaplot they chased. VtR dispensed with lineages because they wanted to run as far and as fast as they could from anything that smelt of Meta, and Fog of Ages existed solely to reinforce that. 2nd Ed. swings the pendulum back a bit by dispensing with Fog and redoing Predator's Taint into Auras. Taint was made expressly to keep play ruthlessly local and prevent globe-spanning adventures (seriously, read The Blood, it's spelled out). So in VtR 1e if you bothered to map your lineage you'd really only care about who was local, because beyond city limits was a big blank area marked &quot;Lycans&quot; and &quot;Here be (Ordo) Dragons!&quot;<br /> <br /> Now as a storyteller I actually like having published characters around. Why? They're not straitjackets--I'm running them and can decide how they act, and whether to use someone if I need a precise reaction. No, they help to &quot;dress&quot; the setting in something recognizable. They're like touchstones that remind the players things are serious for reasons that may not even be in the current story. In other words, established character names in an NPC's lineage act for players the exact same way as they did in olden days: encoded info to help them react faster and more accurately.<br /> <br /> Players become more comfortable and immersed in the setting, and that makes play better. Now if you can spend enough time on worldbuilding that you've replaced all this, then more power to you.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 12-01-2016, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T20:27:07-08:00","id":1010919,"title":"","content":"Just want to point out there wasn't really a metaplot in Masquerade until revised, so six years of Vampire's publication history had no metaplot. It had background information including information about Gehenna, but the only supplements that really advanced any timeline was Chicago by Night 1st edition &gt; Under a Blood Red Moon &gt; Chicago by Night 2nd Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}